		ClearVision

DEFINITIONS:

	(a). 'ClearVision' means the ClearVision software project, including all source code, documentation, assets, and related materials contained within its codebase.

	(b). 'grep' and 'ripgrep' mean the respective text-search utilities known by those names and are referenced solely for comparison, compatibility, or explanatory purposes.

	(c). 'User' means any individual or entity that downloads, executes, studies, modifies, distributes, or otherwise interacts with ClearVision.

	(d). 'Release' means any published version of ClearVision identified by a version number, tag, commit, or distribution package.


ClearVision is a fast, modern, recursive search utility written entirely in C.
It is inspired by grep and ripgrep while exploring alternative approaches to searching, indexing, project exploration, and developer workflows.
The project prioritizes performance, simplicity, maintainability, and developer experience.

Inspired by tools such as grep and ripgrep, ClearVision is primarily focused on performance, simplicity, and efficiency.
grep and ripgrep are both excellent search utilities that have proven themselves across countless workflows and codebases.
ClearVision is not intended to replace them, but rather to explore alternative approaches to recursive searching, indexing,
and result presentation while remaining lightweight and easy to use.

The goal of ClearVision is to provide a fast and intuitive search experience for files, directories, and large projects,
while maintaining the simplicity that makes command-line search tools so valuable.


FEATURES:

	(1). Recursive directory search.

	(2). Single file search.

	(3). Multiple file search.

	(4). Literal string searching.

	(5). Regular expression searching (PCRE2).

	(6). Fuzzy searching.

	(7). Multi-pattern search.

	(8). Case-sensitive and case-insensitive modes.

	(9). Whole-word matching.

	(10). Exact-match mode.

	(11). Match counting.

	(12). Context lines before, after, and around matches.

	(13). Include glob patterns.

	(14). Exclude glob patterns.

	(15). Hidden file control.

	(16). Symlink control.

	(17). Binary file detection and filtering.

	(18). Extension filtering.

	(19). Maximum file size filtering.

	(20). Respect .gitignore.

	(21). Search tracked files.

	(22). Search modified files.

	(23). Search untracked files.

	(24). Standard terminal output.

	(25). Colored output.

	(26). JSON output.

	(27). Tree output.

	(28). Statistics output.

	(29). SQLite-backed indexing.

	(30). Incremental indexing.

	(31). Metadata tracking.

	(32). Indexed searching.

	(33). Index rebuild command.

	(34). Index removal command.

	(35). Multi-threaded operation with configurable thread pool.

	(36). Memory-mapped file support.

	(37). Efficient memory usage.

	(38). Optimized for large repositories.

	(39). Minimal allocations and copies.

	(40). ncurses-based terminal UI.

	(41). Live search.

	(42). Result navigation.

	(43). File preview.

	(44). Real-time filtering.

	(45). Editor launching.


INSTALLATION:

ClearVision uses Just as its build orchestration tool. Ensure you have the following dependencies installed:

	- clang (or gcc)
	- pkg-config
	- sqlite3
	- pcre2
	- ncurses
	- pthreads

BUILD COMMANDS:

	just build
	just release
	just clean
	just install
	just uninstall


NIX:

ClearVision provides a Nix flake for reproducible development and builds:

	nix develop
	nix build
	nix run


USAGE:

BASIC SEARCH:

	cv search "pattern"
	cv regex "pattern"
	cv fuzzy "pattern"

SEARCH OPTIONS:

	cv search "pattern" -i
	cv search "pattern" -w
	cv search "pattern" -c
	cv search "pattern" -A 3
	cv search "pattern" -B 3
	cv search "pattern" -C 3
	cv search "pattern" -j 8

FILE FILTERING:

	cv search "pattern" --hidden
	cv search "pattern" --follow
	cv search "pattern" --include "*.c"
	cv search "pattern" --exclude "*.o"
	cv search "pattern" --max-size 1048576

OUTPUT FORMATS:

	cv search "pattern" --json
	cv search "pattern" --tree
	cv search "pattern" --stats

INDEXING:

	cv index /path/to/project
	cv rebuild
	cv remove-index
	cv stats

INTERACTIVE INTERFACE:

	cv tui

OTHER COMMANDS:

	cv version
	cv help


CONFIGURATION:

ClearVision uses the following filesystem paths:

	- Configuration: ~/.config/clearvision
	- Cache: ~/.cache/clearvision
	- Data: ~/.local/share/clearvision
